<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{DOMAIN}}{{PREFIX}} · getBible query API</title>
{{#IF FAVICON}}<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico">
{{/IF}}<style>{{CSS}}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>{{DOMAIN}}{{#UNLESS IS_ROOT}} <code>{{PREFIX}}</code>{{/UNLESS}}</h1>
<p class="lead">The getBible query endpoint: give it a scripture reference, get the verses. <span class="badge">{{ACCESS_MODE_LABEL}}</span> <span class="badge">API {{VERSION}}</span></p>

<h2>The one route</h2>
<pre><code>GET https://{{DOMAIN}}{{PREFIX}}{translation}/{reference}</code></pre>
{{#IF IS_ROOT}}<p>This domain serves API version {{VERSION}} (Bible data version {{VERSION}}) at its root: there is no version segment in its paths.</p>
{{/IF}}<table>
<tr><th>Part</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Examples</th></tr>
{{#UNLESS IS_ROOT}}<tr><td><code>{{VERSION}}</code></td><td>API version; serves Bible data version {{VERSION}}.</td><td><code>{{VERSION}}</code></td></tr>
{{/UNLESS}}
<tr><td><code>translation</code></td><td>Translation abbreviation.</td><td><code>{{DEFAULT_TRANSLATION}}</code>, <code>aov</code>, <code>vulgate</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>reference</code></td><td>A scripture reference, or several separated by <code>;</code>. Book names, abbreviations, chapters, verses and ranges are all understood.</td><td><code>John3:16</code>, <code>Genesis 1:1-3</code>, <code>Ps23;Mat7:7</code></td></tr>
</table>
<pre><code>curl https://{{DOMAIN}}{{PREFIX}}{{DEFAULT_TRANSLATION}}/John%203:16</code></pre>
<p>The response is a JSON object with one entry per chapter, keyed <code>{translation}_{book}_{chapter}</code>, each holding the translation metadata, the references that selected it, and its verses. Responses carry <code>Cache-Control: public, max-age={{CACHE_SECONDS}}</code> and an <code>ETag</code>{{#IF OPENAPI_URL}}; the full description is in <a href="{{OPENAPI_URL}}">openapi.json</a>{{/IF}}.</p>

<h2>Short forms</h2>
<p>Anything shorter than the full route is a permanent redirect (<code>301</code>) to it. A missing translation becomes <code>{{DEFAULT_TRANSLATION}}</code>; a reference that cannot be resolved becomes <code>{{DEFAULT_REFERENCE}}</code>.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Request</th><th>Redirects to</th></tr>
{{#UNLESS IS_ROOT}}<tr><td><code>/{{VERSION}}</code></td><td><code>{{PREFIX}}{{DEFAULT_TRANSLATION}}/{{DEFAULT_REFERENCE}}</code></td></tr>
{{/UNLESS}}<tr><td><code>{{PREFIX}}aov</code></td><td><code>{{PREFIX}}aov/{{DEFAULT_REFERENCE}}</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>{{PREFIX}}John3:16</code></td><td><code>{{PREFIX}}{{DEFAULT_TRANSLATION}}/John3:16</code></td></tr>
{{#UNLESS IS_ROOT}}<tr><td><code>/aov/John3:16</code></td><td><code>{{PREFIX}}aov/John3:16</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>/John3:16</code></td><td><code>{{PREFIX}}{{DEFAULT_TRANSLATION}}/John3:16</code></td></tr>
{{/UNLESS}}</table>
<p>The full route itself is strict: an unknown translation answers <code>404</code>, an unresolvable reference answers <code>400</code>, and a query string answers <code>400</code>, because this endpoint takes no parameters.</p>

<h2>Access</h2>
{{ACCESS_HTML}}
<p>Documentation pages, <code>openapi.json</code>, <code>GET /healthz</code> and <code>GET /readyz</code> are available without a token. Token checks apply to API data requests.</p>

<h2>Errors</h2>
<p>Every error is an <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457">RFC 9457 problem document</a> (<code>application/problem+json</code>) with <code>type</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>code</code>, <code>detail</code> and <code>instance</code>. The <code>detail</code> field carries the message.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Status</th><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
<tr><td>400</td><td>invalid_reference</td><td>The reference does not resolve.</td></tr>
<tr><td>400</td><td>request_limit</td><td>Too many references or verses in one request.</td></tr>
<tr><td>400</td><td>parameters_not_accepted</td><td>A query string was sent.</td></tr>
<tr><td>401</td><td>unauthorized</td><td>A bearer token is required and was missing or invalid.</td></tr>
<tr><td>404</td><td>translation_not_found</td><td>No such translation.</td></tr>
{{#UNLESS IS_ROOT}}<tr><td>404</td><td>unknown_version</td><td>Only <code>{{VERSION}}</code> is served here.</td></tr>
{{/UNLESS}}<tr><td>429</td><td>rate_limited</td><td>The public budget for your address is used up.</td></tr>
<tr><td>503</td><td>repository_unavailable, readiness_failed</td><td>The Scripture files are temporarily unreadable.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Health</h2>
<p><code>GET /healthz</code> answers when the service is up; <code>GET /readyz</code> answers <code>200</code> only after reading scripture for the configured default reference, or <code>503</code> with a problem document and <code>Retry-After</code> when unavailable. Token-protected responses use <code>Cache-Control: private, no-store</code>.</p>

<p><a href="/">All endpoints of {{DOMAIN}}</a></p>

<footer>Served by getBible · <a href="https://getbible.net">getbible.net</a> · Requests carry an <code>X-Request-ID</code> header; quote it when reporting a problem.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
